Subject: [PATCH] drivers: i2c: shell: a scan the controller cannot do fails

Local patch of this workspace (zephyr/manifest/zephyr/patches.yml), not
meant for upstream.

"i2c scan" probes each address with a write of no bytes and prints "--"
for every error. A controller that cannot send such a write (the
DesignWare driver returns -ENOTSUP for a message of length 0) then made
the command print "0 devices found" and return 0, although devices
answer. When a probe returns -ENOTSUP, the command now stops, prints that
the controller does not support this scan, and returns -ENOTSUP. Any
other error (a NACK: no device at that address) still prints "--".

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/i2c_shell.c b/drivers/i2c/i2c_shell.c
index fa6f6c8..1d83459 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/i2c_shell.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/i2c_shell.c
@@ -70,14 +70,24 @@ static int cmd_i2c_scan(const struct shell *sh, size_t argc, char **argv)
 
 			struct i2c_msg msgs[1];
 			uint8_t dst;
+			int ret;
 
 			/* Send the address to read from */
 			msgs[0].buf = &dst;
 			msgs[0].len = 0U;
 			msgs[0].flags = I2C_MSG_WRITE | I2C_MSG_STOP;
-			if (i2c_transfer(dev, &msgs[0], 1, i + j) == 0) {
+			ret = i2c_transfer(dev, &msgs[0], 1, i + j);
+			if (ret == 0) {
 				shell_fprintf_normal(sh, "%02x ", i + j);
 				++cnt;
+			} else if (ret == -ENOTSUP) {
+				/* The controller cannot send a write of no bytes:
+				 * no address can be probed this way.
+				 */
+				shell_print(sh, "");
+				shell_error(sh, "I2C: %s does not support this scan "
+					    "(zero-length writes)", argv[ARGV_DEV]);
+				return -ENOTSUP;
 			} else {
 				shell_fprintf_normal(sh, "-- ");
 			}
